  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Emma and Anirudh are playing a game on a string.\n\nYou receive a string `s`, Emma and Anirudh will take turns playing the following game where Emma starts **first**:\n\n* On Emma's turn, she has to remove any **non-empty** substring from `s` that includes an **odd** number of vowels.\n* On Anirudh's turn, he has to remove any **non-empty** substring from `s` that includes an **even** number of vowels.\n\nThe first player who cannot make a move on their turn loses the game. We assume that both Emma and Anirudh play **optimally**.\n\nOutput `true` if Emma wins the game, and `false` otherwise.\n\nThe English vowels are: `a`, `e`, `i`, `o`, and `u`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"leetcoder\"\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**  \nEmma can win the game as follows:\n\n* Emma plays first, she can delete the underlined substring in `s = \"leetcoder\"` which includes 3 vowels. The resulting string is `s = \"der\"`.\n* Anirudh plays second, he can delete the underlined substring in `s = \"der\"` which includes 0 vowels. The resulting string is `s = \"er\"`.\n* Emma plays third, she can delete the whole string `s = \"er\"` which includes 1 vowel.\n* Anirudh plays fourth, since the string is empty, there is no valid play for Anirudh. So Emma wins the game.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"bbcd\"\n\n**Output:** false\n\n**Explanation:**  \nThere is no valid play for Emma in her first turn, so Emma loses the game.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 105`\n* `s` consists only of lowercase English letters.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
